<tr><th class="News">10-04</th><td class="News"><a title="GNUSlashLinux is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution featuring the minimalist Noctalia desktop shell on top of the niri Wayland compositor. It is designed specifically for developers and power users seeking a lean, keyboard-driven operating system. The distribution's default software set includes a GPU-accelerated Kitty terminal, the modern Helix text editor, the asynchronous Yazi terminal file manager, the privacy-focused Helium web browser, and the Zathura document viewer. GNUSlashLinux also provides several pre-configured themes and colour schemes, as well as various modern command-line tools as alternatives to classic Unix commands." href="gnuslashlinux">GNUSlashLinux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-03</th><td class="News"><a title="Proton OS is a desktop-oriented Linux distribution based on Debian's &quot;Stable&quot; branch. Featuring the KDE Plasma desktop, it is built with small businesses in mind, designed primarily for office workstations, shared computers and reception systems. It also includes the Calamares system installer and is pre-configured to automatically install all security updates. The project's goal is to give businesses greater control over their computers while reducing dependence on proprietary operating systems and unnecessary data collection." href="proton">Proton OS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-02</th><td class="News"><a title="AI-2 is a minimalist desktop Linux distribution providing a local artificial intelligence (AI) assistant. It is based on Artix Linux, an Arch-derived distribution without the systemd init suite, and uses the Xfce desktop. At first login, a setup wizard detects the user's hardware, assigns a capability tier, installs the matching llama.cpp build (an app that runs the latest open model), downloads a fitting model and calculates an AI score that decides which large language models are recommended. The distribution also provides a custom AI-2 Chat application, available in the menu, that opens a chat page in the web browser; it uses an OpenAI-compatible API on localhost, so no data leave the user's computers." href="ai2">AI-2</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-01</th><td class="News"><a title="LinuxTV is a Debian-based live Linux distribution that turns any personal computer into a television set. It boots into a remote-friendly application launcher which can be navigated from a distance with a smartphone. Available application launchers include  Kodi, Stremio, VLC, Proton VPN, as well as Brave browser, Kitty terminal, qBittorent torrent client and a file manager. Among the available streaming services are YouTube, Disney+, AppleTV+, HBO Max, Hulu, Peacock, Paramount+, Twitch, Crunchyroll, Sony LIV, ZEES, SunNXT and YuppyTV. The project also develops LinuxTVRemote, a mobile controller for LinuxTV which can be installed to any Android smartphone and which connects to the LinuxTV desktop launcher over the WebSocket protocol." href="linuxtv">LinuxTV</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">09-30</th><td class="News"><a title="instantOS is a lightweight, Arch-based Linux distribution featuring instantWM, a custom-built window manager. It is designed primarily for power users. The distribution comes with a range of custom tools and utilities, such as instantARCH (the official instantOS installer), instantCONF (a settings manager), instantMENU (a general-purpose menu), instantASSIST (a set of useful shortcuts), instantSEARCH (a file search interface based on plocate), instantLAUNCH (an AppImage helper), instantLOCK (a lock screen), instantNOTIFY (a notification centre), instantPASS (a graphical applications for pass, the standard UNIX password manager), instantSUPPORT (a utility that provides remote access support for instantOS), instantWALLPAPER (a wallpaper scraper and generator), instantWIDGETS (a set of Conky widgets), and several others." href="instantos">instantOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">09-27</th><td class="News"><a title="Maze Linux is an Arch-based Linux distribution focused on security, privacy and artificial intelligence (AI). It ships a customised and hardened KDE Plasma desktop with defensive and anonymity tools installed and pre-configured. The distribution includes a custom Maze control center for configuring various security, privacy, networking, artificial intelligence, hardening and maintenance options. Some of the other interesting utilities included in Maze Linux are: Maze AI (a local AI assistant), Maze Guard (a per-application outbound firewall), QLAM (an antivirus program), Entropy Shield (a one-click anonymity layer), Maze Cloak (a MAC address randomizer), Haze (a serverless messanger over the Tor protocol), HazeDrop (an anonymous file drop) and Maze Connect (a tool to control the desktop from an Android device)." href="maze">Maze Linux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">09-26</th><td class="News"><a title="Infinity Linux is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution featuring the KDE Plasma desktop. Its primarily focus is on speed, flexibility, compatibility and ease of installation. The distribution uses the Calamares system installer and provides out-of-the-box support for Flatpak packages." href="infinity">Infinity Linux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">09-25</th><td class="News"><a title="ChurrOS is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution for the desktop. It defaults to the Spanish language, offering a choice of two user interfaces - a traditional Xfce desktop with a Whisker menu, or a tiling niri compositor with a custom Waybar bar and the fuzzel applications launcher. It also provides several utilities developed in-house and written in Rust; these include Churros Welcome, Churros Settings, Churros Control Center and Churros Popup. The objective of the project is to build a modern, fast and elegant Linux distribution with its proper identity, branding and useful configuration tools." href="churros">ChurrOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">09-23</th><td class="News"><a title="NagisinnraLinux is a Japanese Linux distribution based on Debian's &quot;Stable&quot; branch. Featuring a lightweight Xfce desktop, it is specifically designed to revive older hardware and provide a snappy and minimal, yet fully functional desktop environment for daily use. The distribution's main features include out-of-the-box support for the Japanese language, advanced memory optimisation, use of zram compression to guarantee smooth multitasking, and removal of unnecessary and redundant services to maximise battery life and CPU responsiveness." href="nagisinnra">NagisinnraLinux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">09-21</th><td class="News"><a title="FlickOS is a minimalist desktop Linux distribution based on Debian &quot;Stable&quot; and featuring the labwc Wayland compositor. It includes Waybar (a customisable Wayland bar), mako (a lightweight Wayland notification daemon), fuzzel (an application launcher and fuzzy finder), foot (a lightweight terminal emulator) and PCManFM (a lightweight and fast file manager). The distribution also offers three desktop layouts, optional window tiling, the Waypaper wallpaper picker and the Calamares system installer. FlickOS ships some popular desktop packages, including the Firefox web browser, the LibreOffice office suite and the VLC media player." href="flickos">FlickOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">09-20</th><td class="News"><a title="MakowiecOS is a desktop Linux distribution based on Debian &quot;Stable&quot; and featuring the Cinnamon desktop. It was conceived as an alternative to heavy and closed-source operating systems, offering simplicity, aesthetics, privacy and solid performance. The distribution can be installed to a hard disk using the standard Calamares system installer." href="makowiecos">MakowiecOS</a></td></tr>
