</td>
        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The Besgnulinux team has announced the release of a new edition of its Debian-based Linux distribution - <a href="besgnulinux">Besgnulinux</a> 1.0 which features the Openbox window manager: "<span class="Quote">It had been a long time since I last tested Openbox. I initially created this version for testing purposes. However, once it turned into such a great system, I thought it would be a good idea to adapt it for general use and share it. Having another window manager as an alternative to JWM offers users a second choice. Getting Openbox to its current state certainly required a lot of effort. After all, Openbox doesn't come with built-in components to function as a standalone system on its own; it is built using various tools and custom configurations. Yet, with the right setup, it can become a fantastic system. That is precisely the beauty of window managers - they allow users to customize the experience to their own liking. This version was born out of that very appreciation. What was done for the Openbox 1.0 release? After experimenting with various panels, I decided that Tint2 was the best fit for Openbox.</span>" Read the rest of the <a href="https://besgnulinux.blogspot.com/2026/10/openbox-10-is-ready-for-use.html">release announcement</a> for more information and screenshots. <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/besgnulinux/files/">Download (MD5)</a>: <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/besgnulinux/files/besgnulinux-openbox-1.0.iso">besgnulinux-openbox-1.0.iso</a> (2,745MB, <a href="table.php?distribution=besgnulinux&pkglist=true&version=1.0#pkglist">pkglist</a>).</td>
