</td>
        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">Greg Martin has announced the release of <a href="mainstream">Mainstream</a> OS 3.0.0, a milestone version of the project's Arch-derived desktop and gaming Linux distribution with a highly customised Hyprland-based desktop. The new release comes with a long list of improvements: "<span class="Quote">A rebuilt Welcome app, smoother gaming with a new Gaming settings page, a hug-style dock and per-monitor wallpapers, with updates and shutdowns that keep your work and your changes safe. The Welcome app has been rebuilt - pick your language, window layout, hot corner and wallpaper, then style the bar, dock and window decorations while a live preview of your desktop updates as you go. Welcome's apps page now fits on one screen, sorted into Play, Create and Work, with anything you already have installed marked. Games run even better out of the box - GameMode (a performance booster) and MangoHud (an on-screen performance display) come installed, and the desktop stays responsive while a game loads from a hard drive. New Gaming page in settings - one switch keeps games smooth while something heavy runs in the background, and two more can help some games stutter less or load faster.</span>" See the detailed <a href="https://mainstreamos.org/#changelog">changelog</a> for a complete list of changes. <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/mainstreamos/files/">Download</a> (<a href="table.php?distribution=mainstream&pkglist=true&version=3.0.0#pkglist">pkglist</a>): <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/mainstreamos/files/3.0.0/mainstream-3.0.0.iso">mainstream-3.0.0.iso</a> (2,990MB, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/mainstreamos/files/3.0.0/mainstream-3.0.0.iso.sha256">SHA256</a>, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/mainstreamos/files/3.0.0/mainstream-3.0.0.iso.sig">signature</a>), <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/mainstreamos/files/legacy-nvidia/3.0.0/mainstream-legacy-nvidia-3.0.0.iso">mainstream-