        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">Umbrel, Inc. has announced the release of <a href="umbrelos">umbrelOS</a> 2.0.0, an updated version of the company's Debian-based Linux distribution designed for home servers, with a web-based user interface and an online app store. It is available for standard 64-bit and Raspberry Pi computers. "<span class="Quote">umbrelOS 2.0 is the biggest update we've ever shipped. It brings a new Photos app, Umbrel apps for iPhone and Mac, Machines for running Windows, Ubuntu, and Android inside your Umbrel, multiple user accounts, an MCP server for AI agents, a new Storage Manager with FailSafe (RAID), downloads from cloud storage, GPU acceleration, an all-new App Store, redesigned Settings, faster Files, redesigned CMD/Ctrl-K search, automatic HTTPS, and hundreds of smaller improvements and bug fixes. New features: Photos - photos and videos on your Umbrel show up in the new Photos app automatically, organized by years, months, and days, with albums, favorites, Live Photos, panoramas, and screenshots; Umbrel for iPhone - the new Umbrel app for iOS backs up your entire camera roll to your Umbrel automatically, in the background, even when the app is closed; Umbrel for Mac - the new Umbrel app for macOS finds your Umbrel automatically and adds it as a drive in Finder, on your local network and over Tailscale; Machines - run Windows, Ubuntu, Debian, Android, and more right inside your Umbrel.</span>" Here are the full <a href="https://github.com/getumbrel/umbrel/releases/tag/2.0.0">release notes</a> as published on the project's GitHub pages. <a href="https://github.com/getumbrel/umbrel/releases/tag/2.0.0">Download</a> (<a href="https://download.umbrel.com/release/2.0.0/SHA256SUMS">SHA256</a>, <a href="https://download.umbrel.com/release/2.0.0/SHA256SUMS.ots">signature</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=umbrelos&pkglist=true&version=2.0.0#pkglist">pkglist</a>): <a href="https://download.umbrel.com/release/2.0.0/umbrelos-amd