        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">Uri Herrera has announced the release of <a href="nitrux">Nitrux</a> 7.0.0, a significant update of the project's Debian-based Linux distribution featuring an immutable base and the Hyprland Wayland compositor: "<span class="Quote">We are pleased to announce the launch of Nitrux 7.0.0. This new version combines the latest software updates, bug fixes, performance improvements and ready-to-use hardware support. We've updated the following components in the distribution: Linux kernel with CachyOS patches (by Nitrux), version 7.2.6; Hyprland to version 0.55.4, all the included Hypr utilities are also updated; NVIDIA Open kernel module to version 615.71.09; Lüv icon theme to version 0.8.9; KDE Frameworks to version 6.26.0; Nitrux Update tool system to version 3.0.3; redesigned the updater interface with MauiKit-style cards for system status, update availability and operation progress; refined update states, progress presentation and toolbar controls, and removed the redundant update button; added branch and commit information to the About dialog and fixed a compile failure; updated the application icon and desktop entry....</span>" Read the rest of the <a href="https://nxos.org/changelog/release-announcement-nitrux-7-0-0/">release announcement</a> for further details. Nitrux 7.0.0 comes in  NVIDIA (cachy-nvopen) and AMD/Intel (liquorix-mesa) variants; here are the <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/nitruxos/files/Release/ISO/">download</a> links (<a href="table.php?distribution=nitrux&pkglist=true&version=7.0.0#pkglist">pkglist</a>): <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/nitruxos/files/Release/ISO/nitrux-contemporary-cachy-nvopen-eefaa320-amd64.iso">nitrux-contemporary-cachy-nvopen-eefaa320-amd64.iso</a> (3,420MB, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/nitruxos/files/Release/SHA512/nitrux-contemporary-cachy-nvopen-eefaa320-amd64.sha512">SHA512</a>, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/nitruxos/files/